cff-version: 1.2.0
message: >-
  If you use All-Japan-Grid, please cite it using the metadata in this file.
  Licensing is dual: the network data under data/ (derived from OpenStreetMap)
  is licensed under ODbL-1.0, while the source code is licensed under MIT.
title: All-Japan-Grid
abstract: >-
  An open-source pipeline that automatically constructs a nationwide Japanese
  transmission grid model from OpenStreetMap (OSM) crowdsourced data. It provides
  bus-level GeoJSON layers (substations, lines, plants) across all 10 regions of
  Japan's dual-frequency system, builds sparse bus admittance matrices (Ybus),
  and supports AC power flow, MILP unit commitment, and transient/N-x stability
  analysis.
type: software
